diff --git a/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md b/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md
index b15844e..592d2f2 100644
--- a/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md
+++ b/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md
@@ -46,6 +46,14 @@ The `browser.new` command opens a separate Browser page in the focused dock pane
 
 The toolbar provides Back, Forward, Reload, Go, and Open in system browser. Web also offers a per-tab sandbox toggle; disabling it is temporary and displays an amber warning with neutral text. Desktop shows the observed page title. After a restart, Browser shows the saved title and URL; Restore or Reload opens that address only when requested.
 
+### Annotation extension points
+
+Browser declares session-scoped list slots `sidebar.right.tab.browser.toolbar` and `sidebar.right.tab.browser.annotations`. Toolbar contributions appear immediately before Reload. Owner props carry the tab ID, known URL, loading state and bounded `annotate(options)` / `cancelAnnotation()` callbacks; they never expose DOM, guest identifiers or an evaluator. Contributions own localized controls, retained annotation queues and any explicit Session submission.
+
+The picker supports element clicks, whitespace points and exact drag rectangles. Holding Space temporarily restores page interaction; spaces in the editor remain text input. Escape, navigation, physical unmount, cancellation and disposal release the picker. Results contain a comment/question intent, note, page identity, viewport, document and viewport rectangles, and bounded DOM candidates; candidates never replace a region's rectangle.
+
+Web requires a cooperating page bridge using the `dsh-browser-annotation-v1` MessageChannel request. The provider enforces the known HTTP(S) origin and page URL and rejects absent bridges or invalid results. Desktop executes only the fixed compiled picker inside its approved webview, validates its JSON result and exposes no Node or Electron capability. The local Desktop annotation implementation requires native product validation before release; these operations do not attach screenshots.
+
